My friend Vince wants to change his name to StarBuck (seriously!). We 
went to the bookstore and found a book on basic name-changing procedures. 
The book is by  Nolo Press and is called: _How to Change Your Name_ 
by David Loeb and David Brown.  It's been very useful so far. We learned that 
there are two basic procedures for folks to change their names: 1) Court 
Petition method,  2) Usage method. 

The Court Petition method is a real pain. 
You have to complete several forms, file papers with the county court, 
have the name change published once a week for four consecutuve weeks in a 
newspaper, check with the court to see if an objection has been filed, 
send a certified copy of the Decree Changing Name to the CA Secretary of 
State, notify agencies and business about your name change.  Note that
all of this is for the state of California- You'd have to get details on
your own state. 

The usage method is to basically just to start using your new name and
slowly get new documents like driver's licenses with the new name. One
big drawback is that you can't get a US Passport with your new name unless
you've used it for 5 years.

So I have a question for folks like Max More, Tom Morrow, Simon! Levy etc.
What method did you use to change your name? (Vince and I have a $5 bet
riding on this.)

